  "description": "EZEZUG crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C132 H200 Dy12 N6 O68 2-,5(C1 H4 O1),3(Na1 1+),H1 O1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.821-3.980 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.05-112.34°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C137H213Dy12N6Na3O74. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
